  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:99031",
  "description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: hold event_mutex while checkpointing CRIU events (CVE-2026-74446)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: fix SMI event cross-process information leak (CVE-2026-97422)\n  * kernel: drm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy (CVE-2026-97427)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds for allocate_sdma_queue restore_sdma_id (CVE-2026-97497)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: validate and share PSP fw_pri_buf copies via psp_copy_fw (CVE-2026-97494)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds on allocate_doorbell (CVE-2026-97495)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: Bound GPIO I2C table entry count from VBIOS (CVE-2026-97493)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: fix buffer overflow during vBIOS update (CVE-2026-97425)\n  * kernel: net/smc: protect clcsock lifetime in smc_getname (CVE-2026-99032)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via use-after-free race condition in SCSI tape driver (CVE-2026-99156)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * soft lockup occurs during iomap_finish_ioends (JIRA:RHEL-258946)\n  * gfs2: BUG during withdraw [AlmaLinux-8] (JIRA:RHEL-298310)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
  "issued_date": {
    "$date": 1794355200000
  },
